meta {
  name: POST /api/pan/torg/{torgId}/additional
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/pan/torg/:torgId/additional
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  torgId: 7869
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{adminStaticToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "panNumber": "",
    "holderName": "",
    "phone": "",
    "isSoleProprietor": true,
    "businessName": ""
  }
}

docs {
  `PANCardResource.createAdditionalPANCard` (plutus-java `onboarding/controller/PANCardResource.java:438`), called as VAHN_ADMIN.
  Adds a second PAN to an existing torg and verifies it with the PAN provider in the same call (a paid provider call).
  - `panNumber` must not exist on any PAN yet.
  - `phone` is required and must not be on any other PAN, in any torg. It becomes the IOCL customer mobile
    when the first IOCL card is created for a truck on this PAN, so it must also be new to IOCL.
  - Errors come back as HTTP 400 with the message as a plain string.
  Next step: move the trucks onto the new PAN (`admin-static-token/common/truck/attach-trucks-to-pan.bru`), then create cards.
}
